ency:**.\n   - We need to check if the statement is consistent with the given information.\n   - Consider the scenario where George likes music (\\( L \\)) and has access to a program (\\( P \\)):.\n     - Since \\( L \\rightarrow W \\), George wants to compose (\\( W \\)).\n     - Since \\( P \\rightarrow C \\), George can compose (\\( C \\)).\n     - Since \\( (C \\land W) \\rightarrow F \\), George will compose (\\( F \\)).\n\n   - Now, let\'s consider the scenario where George will not compose (\\( \\neg F \\)):.\n     - If George will not compose, then \\( \\neg F \\) is true.\n     - However, from the given information, we know that if George can compose (\\( C \\)) and wants to compose (\\( W \\)), he will compose (\\( F \\)).\n     - Therefore, if George can compose (\\( C \\)), he must want to compose (\\( W \\)), and thus he will compose (\\( F \\)). Therefore, my final option is: ']]
