messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNo students who work in the library are from the computer science department. All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library. All students who take the database course are from the computer science department. All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course. All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David. James is a student working in the lab. Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? James does not have a part-time job offered by the university.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nTo determine whether the statement "James does not have a part-time job offered by the university" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given information, let\'s break down the information step by step:\n\n1. **No students who work in the library are from the computer science department.**\n   - This means that if someone works in the library, they cannot be from the computer science department.\n\n2. **All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library.**\n   - This implies that if a student has a part-time job offered by the university, they must also be working in the library.\n\n3. **All students who take the database course are from the computer science department.**\n   - This means that if a student takes the database course, they must be from the computer science department.\n\n4. **All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.**\n   - This implies that if a student is instructed by professor David, they must be taking the database course.\n\n5. **All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David.**\n   - This means that if a student is working in the lab, they must be instructed by professor David.\n\n6. **James is a student working in the lab.**\n   - This means that James is working in the lab.\n\n7. **Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.**\n   - This means that Jack does not have a part-time job offered by the university and does not work in the lab.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the information step by step:\n\n- Since James is working in the lab (from point 6), and all students working in the lab are instructed by professor David (from point 5), it follows that James is instructed by professor David.\n- Since all students instructed by professor David are taking the database course (from point 4), it follows that James is taking the database course.\n- Since all students who take the database course are from the computer science department (from point 3), it follows that James is from the computer science department.\n- Since no students who work in the library are from the computer science department (from point 1), and James is working in the lab (from point 6), it follows that James cannot be working in the library.\n- Since all students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library (from point 2), and James is not working in the library (from the previous step), it follows that James does not have a part-time job offered by the university.\n\nTherefore, the statement "James does not have a part-time job offered by the university" is true based on the given information.\n\n<｜User｜>The statement is true.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
