he campus dining halls.\n   - Mary works in student jobs on campus and needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition.\n\n2. **Determine Mary\'s Situation:**.\n   - Since Mary works in student jobs on campus, we know from the first piece of information that she needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition.\n   - This means Mary either orders takeout frequently in college or enjoys the dining hall meals and recipes.\n   - However, we don\'t have enough information to determine which of these two options is true for Mary. Therefore, we cannot definitively say whether she orders takeout frequently or enjoys the dining hall meals and recipes.\n\n3. **Evaluate the Statement:**.\n   - The statement claims that Mary is not a picky eater and spends a lot of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.\n   - To evaluate this statement, we need to consider both scenarios:.\n     - If Mary orders takeout frequently, then she would be a picky eater because she is not enjoying the dining hall meals and recipes.\n     - If Mary enjoys the dining hall meals and recipes, then she would not be a picky eater and would spend a lot of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.\n\n4. **Conclusion:**.\n   - Since we do not have enough information to determine which scenario is true for Mary, we cannot definitively say whether the statement is true, false, or uncertain.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
