ears large shoes, they wear large-sized clothes.).\n     - \\( \\neg LS \\) (Yuri does not wear large-size clothes.).\n\n   - Combining these statements, we get:.\n     - \\( \\neg A \\rightarrow B \\).\n     - \\( B \\rightarrow T \\).\n     - \\( T \\rightarrow L \\).\n     - \\( L \\rightarrow LS \\).\n     - \\( \\neg LS \\).\n\n   - From \\( \\neg LS \\), we know that Yuri does not wear large-sized clothes. This implies that Yuri does not wear large shoes (\\( \\neg L \\)) because \\( L \\rightarrow LS \\).\n\n   - Since \\( \\neg L \\), it follows that Yuri is not tall (\\( \\neg T \\)) because \\( T \\rightarrow L \\).\n\n   - Therefore, if Yuri is not an American basketball player (\\( \\neg A \\)), he cannot be a basketball player (\\( \\neg B \\)) because being a basketball player requires being tall (\\( T \\)).\n\n   - Hence, the statement "If Yuri is not an American basketball player, then Yuri is a basketball player" is false.\n\n4. **Conclusion:**. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
