very busy with their regular jobs grew up as only children with no siblings.\n   - Households with a high net income have people who have parents who are very busy with their regular jobs.\n   - Peter is either both a person who spills a lot of food on his clothing and grew up as an only child with no siblings, or he is neither a person who spills a lot of food on his clothing nor grew up as an only child with no siblings.\n\n2. **Statement Breakdown**:\n   - The statement claims that Peter is either a foodie who goes out frequently to find new food restaurants to try and belongs to a household with a high net income, or he is a foodie who goes out frequently to find new food restaurants to try and does not belong to a household with a high net income.\n\n3. **Logical Reasoning**:\n   - From the context, we know that if Peter spills a lot of food on his clothing, he is a foodie who goes out frequently to find new food restaurants to try.\n   - If Peter grew up as an only child with no siblings, he tidies his spaces consistently and enjoys the process of cleaning.\n   - Since households with a high net income have people who have parents who are very busy with their regular jobs, and Peter is either both a person who spills a lot of food on his clothing and grew up as an only child with no siblings, or he is neither a person who spills a lot of food on his clothing nor grew up as an only child with no siblings, it follows that Peter cannot belong to a household with a high net income if he spills a lot of food on his clothing and grew up as an only child with no siblings.\n   - Therefore, Peter cannot belong to a household with a high net income if he spills a lot of food on his clothing and grew up as an only child with no siblings.\n\n4. **Conclusion**:\n   - The statement is true because Peter cannot belong to a household with a high net income if he spills a lot of food on his clothing and grew up as an only child with no siblings.\n\n<｜User｜>The statement is true.\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
