 to Spanish, it follows that German must also be an Indo-European language.\n- However, the question specifically asks if German is a Romance language, not an Indo-European language.\n\nTherefore, based on the information provided, the correct answer is:\n- **B) False**\n\nGerman is not a Romance language because it is related to Spanish, which is a Romance language, but German itself is not classified as a Romance language. It is part of the Germanic language family, which is distinct from the Romance language family.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
